[size=6][b]Combat Sounds Overhaul Overhauled[/b][/size]

A replacement script for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53859]Combat Sounds Overhaul[/url] (CSO) by Jyggalagpuff. Swings and armor hits still play CSO's sounds, but:

[list]
[*]The sounds are picked for the weapon and for what it hits, rather than at random.
[*]It reacts to attacks and hits as they happen, rather than checking every actor for sounds every frame.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Requires [b]OpenMW 0.51[/b] or newer.
[*]Requires [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53859]Combat Sounds Overhaul[/url] 2.0[/b]. Keep it installed, because its sounds are played from there.
[*]Load this mod [b]below[/b] CSO. There's nothing new to enable: CSO's plugin loads the replaced script.
[*]Remove the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/58744]CSO Optimization Patch[/url] if you have it. It replaces the same file.
[/list]

New to OpenMW mods? [url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]Read this first[/url].

[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]

[b]Options → Scripts → Combat Sounds Overhaul Overhauled[/b] has [b]Hit Volume[/b] and [b]Swing Volume[/b], each from 0 to 1.

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Weapon swishes and armor hit sounds are replaced with CSO's, at a slightly random pitch. Fists and creatures' claws and bites keep the vanilla swish.
[*]Hits that land on no armor get a CSO impact on top of the body hit.
[/list]

[b]Swings:[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Daggers:[/b] sharp metallic and ringing blade, 30% plain.
[*][b]One-handed swords:[/b] ringing blade and metallic blade, 30% plain.
[*][b]Two-handed swords:[/b] metallic blade, 30% plain.
[*][b]Axes:[/b] heavy metallic, 30% plain.
[*][b]Maces, warhammers:[/b] heavy metallic 50%, plain 50%.
[*][b]Staves, spear chops and slashes:[/b] plain 50%, metallic blade 40%, heavy metallic 10%.
[*][b]Spear thrusts:[/b] metallic blade and ringing blade, 30% plain.
[*][b]Thrown weapons:[/b] sharp metallic and plain.
[/list]

[b]Hits:[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Flesh, light armor:[/b] flesh impacts for the weapon, with slices for daggers, stabs for swords, thrusts and arrows, and punchy metallic ones for all but fists and arrows.
[*][b]Medium and heavy armor:[/b] an armor impact with the wearer's flesh sound under it, or a punchy metallic impact.
[*][b]Dwemer machines:[/b] heavy armor impacts.
[*][b]Skeletons, ghosts:[/b] bone hits. Thrusts get a pure stab, and maces, warhammers and staves a pure blunt hit or a blunt bone hit. A pure hit always has a bone hit under it: bone is their flesh.
[/list]

Blades, axes, maces and warhammers also ring on top of a quarter of their hits, except thrusts.

[size=5][b]Creature sounds[/b][/size]

Sounds in [font=Courier New]Sound/Fx/Item/CSOOCreature/<Class>/[/font], from this or any later mod, play on top of every hit a creature of that class takes. The classes are:

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Ghost[/font], [font=Courier New]Skeleton[/font] or [font=Courier New]Metal[/font], from the creature's body.
[*][font=Courier New]Creatures[/font], [font=Courier New]Daedra[/font], [font=Courier New]Undead[/font] or [font=Courier New]Humanoid[/font], from its record.
[/list]

When a creature has two classes, the one from its body is used if its folder has sounds. The folders start out empty.

[size=5][b]For developers[/b][/size]

Every actor has [font=Courier New]I.CombatSoundsOO[/font]. It's per actor, so call it from a script attached after this one, on every actor it should affect.

[code]local cso = I.CombatSoundsOO

cso.emit('Heavy Armor Hit', { weapon = someMace })  -- swap a vanilla sound, as CSO does when it catches one
cso.playSwing(cso.WEAPON.AxeTwoHanded, 0.8)         -- weapon, volume
cso.playHit(cso.ARMOR.Heavy, 1, cso.WEAPON.Blunt)   -- armor, volume, weapon, attack type

cso.setWeaponKind('my_katana', cso.WEAPON.LongBladeTwoHanded)  -- nil to undo
cso.addSwingGroupsHandler(function(recordId)
    if recordId == 'my_katar' then return { cso.SWING_GROUPS.sharpMetal } end
    if recordId == 'my_cestus' then return { cso.SWING_GROUPS.plain }, true end  -- a fist's swish and a whoosh
end)
cso.addOnPlayHandler(function(info)
    if info.weaponId == 'my_katar' then info.volume = info.volume * 0.75 end
    if info.file:find('hit69') then return false end  -- stop this one
end)[/code]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]emit(tag, options)[/font]: [font=Courier New]tag[/font] is one of [font=Courier New]TAGS[/font], the vanilla sound ids CSO answers. [font=Courier New]options[/font] can hold [font=Courier New]weapon[/font], [font=Courier New]attacker[/font], [font=Courier New]attackType[/font], [font=Courier New]volume[/font], [font=Courier New]pitch[/font], and [font=Courier New]force[/font] to play even when no group fits. It returns the file played, or [font=Courier New]nil[/font]. [font=Courier New]pickFile(tag, options)[/font] returns the file without playing it.
[*][font=Courier New]playSwing(weapon, volume, attackType)[/font] and [font=Courier New]playHit(armor, volume, weapon, attackType)[/font] play a sound with no vanilla sound to replace. [font=Courier New]WEAPON[/font] and [font=Courier New]ARMOR[/font] are enums of names, and a misspelled name is an error.
[*][font=Courier New]setWeaponKind(recordId, weapon)[/font] makes a weapon sound like another kind of [font=Courier New]WEAPON[/font].
[*][font=Courier New]addSwingGroupsHandler(handler)[/font] lets a weapon keep its kind but swing with other groups. The handler gets the weapon's record id and returns a list of [font=Courier New]SWING_GROUPS[/font], or [font=Courier New]nil[/font] to leave the weapon to its kind. An empty list keeps the vanilla swish. Return [font=Courier New]true[/font] after the list to keep the vanilla swish as well, with CSO's whoosh on top (after [font=Courier New]nil[/font], the kind's).
[*][font=Courier New]addOnPlayHandler(handler)[/font] is called with [font=Courier New]info[/font] before every sound. [font=Courier New]file[/font], [font=Courier New]volume[/font] and [font=Courier New]pitch[/font] can be changed. The volume settings apply on top. It also has [font=Courier New]kind[/font] ('swing' or 'hit'), [font=Courier New]tag[/font], [font=Courier New]weapon[/font], [font=Courier New]weaponId[/font], [font=Courier New]armor[/font], [font=Courier New]attackType[/font], [font=Courier New]category[/font], [font=Courier New]layered[/font], [font=Courier New]underneath[/font] and [font=Courier New]via[/font]. Return [font=Courier New]false[/font] to stop the sound. The vanilla one stays stopped, unless the swing groups handler kept it.
[*][font=Courier New]getBody()[/font] and [font=Courier New]getCreatureClasses()[/font] say what the actor counts as. [font=Courier New]setDebug(true)[/font] logs every sound it plays.
[*]Global scripts can send the actor these events: [font=Courier New]CombatSoundsOO_Emit[/font] ([font=Courier New]tag[/font] plus [font=Courier New]emit[/font]'s options), [font=Courier New]_PlaySwing[/font], [font=Courier New]_PlayHit[/font] and [font=Courier New]_SetWeaponKind[/font], with the same arguments as fields.
[/list]

To try it, click an NPC in the console, type [font=Courier New]luas[/font], then run [font=Courier New]I.CombatSoundsOO.emit('Heavy Armor Hit')[/font].

[size=5][b]Credits[/b][/size]

[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53859]Combat Sounds Overhaul[/url] and its sounds are by Jyggalagpuff, made from Impact Sounds. The script is by Max Yari.
